          "id": "7a92837302b6668bfa1fa7fb182808d69a61766a",
          "message": "peerset/metrics: Add notification layer metrics for peer states (#11574)\n\nThis PR adds two new metrics to enhance our monitoring insights into the\nnotification protocol.\n\nThe data exposed:\n- connected peers grouped by in / out and kind (reserve / non-reserve)\n- disconnected and backed off peers \n\nBecause the slot counts are tightly coupled with the full peerset state\nmachine, I've picked an eventually consistent model to easily bump the\nmetrics at 1s tick intervals.\n\n\n## Dashboards\n\n- PR been deployed on collators here:\nhttps://grafana.teleport.parity.io/goto/j_BY2IpvR?orgId=1\n\nThe following dashboard shows how many peers are backedoff on the\ncollation protocol:\n\n<img width=\"3010\" height=\"1635\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-04-01 at 17 15 46\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20ece572-7ddf-42c2-944f-5839d0508f43\"\n/>\n\nThe following dashboard shows how many peers are connected (and reserved\n/ unreserved):\n<img width=\"3006\" height=\"1639\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-04-01 at 17 15 20\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8781d40b-e911-4218-912b-b9be7e76efe7\"\n/>\n\n\nPart of:\n- https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/11377\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Alexandru Vasile <alexandru.vasile@parity.io>\nCo-authored-by: cmd[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
